    "mandatory_policy": "ADC1 emits Dedicated for its exclusive IRQ12; ADC2 emits SharedDac for shared ADC2_DAC IRQ30. There is no policy-free L012 async macro route.",
    "IRQ_identity": "Exactly one ADC1, ADC2, DAC and SYSCTRL; exact own-L012 addresses, register kind/version/block; unique IRQ12/30 by name and number; complete IRQ30 owner/link set is ADC2 GLOBAL and DAC GLOBAL.",
    "register_geometry": "All14 DAC scalar registers accounted for, full14-field CR0 equality, CR1 and mixed DOR geometry; ADC IER/ISR/ICR exact offset/access/field sets including reserved bit2 preservation.",
    "rcc_control": "Authoritative real DAC APBEN2/APBRST2 bit10 domain, key0x5A5A at31:16, gate active true/reset asserted false, no shared group; common ADC1-ADC2 APBEN1/APBRST1 bit0 domain remains distinct. No DAC analog kernel clock invented.",
    "checker_delta": "One existing finite checker extended; original39 pre-receipt AST nodes preserved. No HAL-string assertions, models, fake peripherals, build subprocess or permanent historical canonical hash gate.",
    "source_lock": "Exactly15 evidence-consumer appends; reversing their exact pointers restores complete prior parsed lock, including all order and unrelated values. No original/member/text identity, archive chain, URL, provenance, pin history or license change.",
    "current_source_identity": "Independently verified15 selected cache artifacts and8 original archive chains;43 PDF pages re-extracted and matched pinned text exactly. Current EN manual is the selected identity from the immutable hardware proof.",
    "independent_geometry": "Actual own SVD matches current18 ADC registers94 fields, with existing manual ISR RO correction, and14 DAC registers34 fields. All3 selections have exact interrupt and RCC domains.",
    "safe_API_closure": "Current DAC preparation/start full writes produce both IEs0; set/read do not write IEs; Drop preserves them. OPA only retains gate and reads DAC; RCC mutation remains private/init-only; safe DMA has SRAM or fixed serial destinations. Raw writers and arbitrary faults are outside this functional contract.",
    "interpretation_boundaries": "Masked stale DAC flags allowed; EN/OUT/TEN/WAVE/DMAEN are not IRQ masks. No DAC control/data/status writes or reset/gate-off are added. Gate-opening progress is a conservative policy inference, not a proven APBEN2-to-DOR transfer event. Future safe DAC IRQ/trigger/DMA or public RCC mutation needs re-review."
